WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:41.560
[Music]

00:00:42.560 --> 00:01:00.660
[A group of teens assembles, climbs into their cars, 
and heads to the movies.]

00:01:01.220 --> 00:01:04.840
[Tires screech as car drives off.]

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:46.080
[Music]

00:01:46.266 --> 00:01:48.200
[Betty:] Thanks, Don.

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:49.100
[Don:] Ready to go now?

00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:52.466
[Mrs. Turner:] Betty, you and Don aren't leaving 
are you? It isn't late.

00:01:52.466 --> 00:01:56.732
[Betty:] Well, I think we'd better, Mrs. Turner. But 
we had a wonderful time. Thank you so much.

00:01:56.733 --> 00:02:01.499
[Don:] That's the trouble with going steady with a 
girl like Betty, Mrs. Turner. Her mother always 
expects her home by 11.

00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:04.433
[Mrs. Turner:] Well, you come back again.

00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:08.100
[Betty:] Uh-huh. We will.

00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:17.700
[Mrs. Turner:] Good night.
[Betty:] Good night.

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:33.366
[Music]

00:02:33.366 --> 00:02:36.266
[Don:] Kind of quiet tonight.
[Betty:] Uh-huh.

00:02:36.266 --> 00:02:40.332
[Music]

00:02:40.333 --> 00:02:41.833
[Betty:] Don?
[Don:] Hm-hm?

00:02:41.833 --> 00:02:49.333
[Betty:] You know what? I've never felt about 
anyone, well, the way I feel about you.

00:02:49.333 --> 00:02:54.999
[Don:] Gosh, Betty. I think you're wonderful too.

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:58.066
[Betty:] Hey, you better watch out [laughter]. You're 
getting on the wrong side of the road.

00:02:58.066 --> 00:02:59.866
[Don:] We oughta pull off the road for a few minutes.

00:02:59.866 --> 00:03:03.566
[Betty:] Well, I have to be home by 11, remember? 
Uh-huh. [laughter].

00:03:03.566 --> 00:03:06.432
[Don:] Okay.

00:03:06.433 --> 00:03:09.566
[Music]

00:03:09.566 --> 00:03:12.299
[Don:] Are you sure you have to be home right 
away?

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:19.933
[Betty:] Well...oh, I guess not. Not for a while 
anyway.

00:03:19.933 --> 00:03:49.166
[Music]

00:03:49.166 --> 00:04:18.099
[Don and Betty are sitting in the car; Betty is 
tearful.]

00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:21.466
[Don:] Betty.

00:04:21.466 --> 00:04:25.332
[Betty:] Let's go home, Don.

00:04:25.333 --> 00:04:28.166
[Don:] Okay.

00:04:28.166 --> 00:04:55.532
[Music]

00:04:55.533 --> 00:04:57.933
[Nicky:] Hey, Don, boy. What's the matter? Looks 
like you got deep thoughts.

00:04:57.933 --> 00:05:00.433
[Don:] Oh, just thinking something, Nicky. That's 
all. Just thinking.

00:05:00.433 --> 00:05:06.099
[Nicky:] Still dreaming about the little queen over in 
the city? Did Betty find you a changed man?

00:05:06.100 --> 00:05:10.700
[Don:] Hey, you come off that right now. Listen, 
Betty's not that kind of girl and you remember it.

00:05:10.700 --> 00:05:28.233
[Nicky:] Okay. Okay. Just forget I mentioned it.

00:05:28.233 --> 00:05:33.333
[Don:] Say, Nicky?
[Nicky:] Yeah.

00:05:33.333 --> 00:05:34.699
[Don:] You know those girls in the city the other 
night?

00:05:34.700 --> 00:05:36.300
[Nicky:] Yeah.

00:05:36.300 --> 00:05:37.533
[Don:] You think they might have had something?

00:05:37.533 --> 00:05:43.866
[Nicky:] You bet they did. Oh, oh, you mean... No, just forget about it, buddy.

00:05:43.866 --> 00:05:47.332
They're just a couple of good kids who want to 
have a little fun.

00:05:47.333 --> 00:05:51.066
[Don:] Well, I don't know, Nicky. Something happened.

00:05:51.066 --> 00:05:53.532
[Nicky:] What do you mean something happened?

00:05:53.533 --> 00:05:57.699
[Don:] Well, I've got some sort of sore down there.

00:05:57.700 --> 00:06:02.533
[Nicky:] Oh, don't worry about it. It's probably just a 
pimple or something.

00:06:02.533 --> 00:06:06.433
The same thing happened to me and it cleared up 
all by itself.

00:06:06.433 --> 00:06:10.799
[Don:] Well, maybe. But I think I'll have to go see a 
doctor just to be sure.

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:14.566
[Nicky:] Well, suit yourself. Personally, I'd just 
forget all about it.

00:06:14.566 --> 00:06:30.366
[Music]

00:06:30.366 --> 00:06:36.566
[Dr. Carlson:] Well, there they are.

00:06:36.566 --> 00:06:49.866
Take a look at this.

00:06:49.866 --> 00:06:53.199
[Don:] Is it something bad, Dr. Carlson? Do you 
know what it is?

00:06:53.200 --> 00:06:56.600
[Dr. Carlson:] Well there's no doubt about what it 
is, Don.

00:06:56.600 --> 00:07:00.533
Those little corkscrew things are the germs of 
syphilis.

00:07:00.533 --> 00:07:04.333
[Don:] Syphilis? Gosh, doctor, I...

00:07:04.333 --> 00:07:10.899
[Dr. Carlson:] Now, take it easy. It isn't the end of 
the world for you.

00:07:10.900 --> 00:07:15.333
We can cure syphilis, especially if we find it in the 
early stages such as yours.

00:07:15.333 --> 00:07:18.599
[Don:] Are you sure it's syphilis, doctor?

00:07:18.600 --> 00:07:22.000
[Dr. Carlson:] The darkfield examination is proof 
enough.

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:24.966
We'll also run a blood test on you before you 
leave.

00:07:24.966 --> 00:07:28.766
[Don:] I don't know. I don't know how I got it. I 
haven't done anything.

00:07:28.766 --> 00:07:33.832
[Dr. Carlson:] Don, let's be straightforward about 
this. I'm not here to make a moral judgment,

00:07:33.833 --> 00:07:38.733
but you and I know that it was contracted through 
sexual intercourse with an infected person.

00:07:38.733 --> 00:07:45.099
[Don:] Well, I heard you could get something like 
this from a toilet seat or something.

00:07:45.100 --> 00:07:49.000
[Dr. Carlson:] About as much chance as being hit 
by a meteor.

00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:50.933
[Don:] What am I going to tell my dad?

00:07:50.933 --> 00:07:57.599
[Dr. Carlson:] The best thing is to tell him the truth.

00:07:57.600 --> 00:08:03.933
I'll talk to him if you want me to.

00:08:03.933 --> 00:08:12.099
Don, there are some things you should know about 
this disease of yours.

00:08:12.100 --> 00:08:16.666
Now here we are. This is the sore you have, Don.

00:08:16.666 --> 00:08:20.932
It's called a chancre. It is usually painless.

00:08:20.933 --> 00:08:26.066
Sometimes it looks like this. And sometimes like 
this.

00:08:26.066 --> 00:08:32.766
When it appears on or around your sexual organs, 
you've probably got what we call primary syphilis.

00:08:32.766 --> 00:08:36.032
[Don:] Boy. It's pretty awful looking.

00:08:36.033 --> 00:08:39.799
[Dr. Carlson:] Well now, actually the appearance of 
a chancre is rather fortunate.

00:08:39.800 --> 00:08:42.100
Sometimes a sore does not appear.

00:08:42.100 --> 00:08:44.533
Or it's so small that you wouldn't notice it.

00:08:44.533 --> 00:08:47.766
Now, when that happens the disease might go 
unnoticed for years.

00:08:47.766 --> 00:08:51.699
[Don:] Well, what happens if you don't find it right 
away?

00:08:51.700 --> 00:08:55.166
[Dr. Carlson:] Well, the results can be tragic in 
many instances.

00:08:55.166 --> 00:09:01.032
Syphilis can cripple you. Blind you. Destroy your 
brain.

00:09:01.033 --> 00:09:03.766
And, of course, it may kill you eventually.

00:09:03.766 --> 00:09:07.632
[Don:] Well, you did say it could be cured though, 
especially in an early case like mine.

00:09:07.633 --> 00:09:11.733
[Dr. Carlson:] Yes. In the stage you have we can 
knock out the spirochete in a hurry.

00:09:11.733 --> 00:09:14.999
[Don:] Spirochete? What's that?

00:09:15.000 --> 00:09:18.566
[Dr. Carlson:] Well, that's the corkscrew-shaped 
thing that you saw on the microscope.

00:09:18.566 --> 00:09:20.766
Like this.

00:09:20.766 --> 00:09:24.699
These germs enter the body when you have 
sexual intercourse.

00:09:24.700 --> 00:09:26.566
They burrow under the skin.

00:09:26.566 --> 00:09:30.699
Usually causing a chancre to appear where they 
entered.

00:09:30.700 --> 00:09:35.133
They work their way into the blood stream and the 
chancre on the skin disappears.

00:09:35.133 --> 00:09:41.366
Now, that happens to quite a few people who think 
they're all right after the sore clears up.

00:09:41.366 --> 00:09:46.632
Now Don, I'll have to have the names of the girls 
you had sexual relations with.

00:09:46.633 --> 00:09:48.866
And, naturally, this is confidential.

00:09:48.866 --> 00:09:54.566
[Don:] There haven't exactly been dozens. As a 
matter of fact, I know exactly where I got it.

00:09:54.566 --> 00:09:58.799
There was this one girl over in the city, Barbara 
Meyers.

00:09:58.800 --> 00:10:01.833
[Dr. Carlson:] Well now, tell me everything you can 
about this girl, Don.

00:10:01.833 --> 00:10:05.299
You see, the Health Department over there will 
want to contact her to see that she's examined

00:10:05.300 --> 00:10:08.400
and treated before she gives the disease to 
someone else.

00:10:08.400 --> 00:10:10.600
[Don:] I'm afraid I don't know her address. As a 
matter of fact,

00:10:10.600 --> 00:10:14.366
I'm not even sure that's her real name.

00:10:14.366 --> 00:10:15.299
[Dr. Carlson:] Anybody else, Don?

00:10:15.300 --> 00:10:19.333
[Don:] No, sir. Just that one girl.

00:10:19.333 --> 00:10:21.199
[Dr. Carlson:] Are you being honest with me, Don?

00:10:21.200 --> 00:10:25.933
[Don:] I told you. There's this one girl over in the 
city and that's it.

00:10:25.933 --> 00:10:28.099
[Dr. Carlson:] Now, look here son.

00:10:28.100 --> 00:10:32.466
I've admired your courage for coming in here and 
facing up to the facts.

00:10:32.466 --> 00:10:36.166
But you get it through your head that you're 
dealing with a deadly disease.

00:10:36.166 --> 00:10:39.566
Not some common cold or a case of the chicken 
pox.

00:10:39.566 --> 00:10:43.899
If you think you're doing some girl a favor by 
protecting her good name and reputation,

00:10:43.900 --> 00:10:46.466
you're wrong. You're terribly wrong.

00:10:46.466 --> 00:10:51.232
[Don:] I've said all there is to say. There is no other 
girl.

00:10:51.233 --> 00:10:57.066
[Dr. Carlson:] All right. If there's no other girl, we'll 
leave it at that.

00:10:57.066 --> 00:11:00.166
But before we do, I want to show you something.

00:11:00.166 --> 00:11:03.666
Now, come here.

00:11:03.666 --> 00:11:07.899
I've showed you the symptoms of syphilis as they 
appear in the male.

00:11:07.900 --> 00:11:13.066
Generally the chancre appears on or around the 
external sex organ.

00:11:13.066 --> 00:11:19.232
Men and  boys who contract syphilis have a good chance of spotting it when the danger appears.

00:11:19.233 --> 00:11:22.666
With a girl, however, it 's not quite as easy.

00:11:22.666 --> 00:11:26.566
You see, a girl could develop a chancre way up 
inside like this,

00:11:26.566 --> 00:11:29.432
and never know that she had syphilis.

00:11:29.433 --> 00:11:33.333
Of course, if she's lucky, it will appear out in the 
open like this.

00:11:33.333 --> 00:11:36.299
Now we don't have to worry about this. 
do we, Don?

00:11:36.300 --> 00:11:40.533
You say there's no other girl who might have 
become infected by you.

00:11:40.533 --> 00:11:45.333
[Don:] Even if a girl had it and didn't know it, she'd 
find out, wouldn't she?

00:11:45.333 --> 00:11:47.099
I mean, there'd be other signs.

00:11:47.100 --> 00:11:52.333
[Dr. Carlson:] Yes. Yes, sometimes there are other 
signs.

00:11:52.333 --> 00:11:58.099
In the secondary stage, a few weeks or months 
after the primary chancre disappears,

00:11:58.100 --> 00:12:00.166
she may develop a sore throat.

00:12:00.166 --> 00:12:02.166
Patches of her hair may come out.

00:12:02.166 --> 00:12:06.132
Or her skin may break out in a rash like this.

00:12:06.133 --> 00:12:11.333
Then again, the symptoms of secondary syphilis 
may be so slight that they go unnoticed.

00:12:11.333 --> 00:12:17.199
If she doesn't go to a doctor, or if a doctor isn't 
looking for syphilis, it may never be detected.

00:12:17.200 --> 00:12:21.633
You see, the secondary symptoms, like a primary 
chancre,

00:12:21.633 --> 00:12:24.033
also will disappear even without treatment.

00:12:24.033 --> 00:12:27.266
[Don:] Well, you'd find it for sure when you had a 
blood test before you got married.

00:12:27.266 --> 00:12:28.699
They'd discover it then.

00:12:28.700 --> 00:12:32.233
[Dr. Carlson:] Now, that would be a lovely wedding 
present for a girl to discover

00:12:32.233 --> 00:12:35.999
that she had syphilis a few days before the 
wedding.

00:12:36.000 --> 00:12:40.500
And in some states some people can get married 
even without a blood test.

00:12:40.500 --> 00:12:43.433
But suppose she had undetected syphilis?

00:12:43.433 --> 00:12:45.833
Inactive in the latent stages.

00:12:45.833 --> 00:12:50.733
She might go for years thinking that she's all right.

00:12:50.733 --> 00:12:56.266
Then before she knows what's happening to her, 
she goes insane or becomes a hopeless cripple.

00:12:56.266 --> 00:12:58.032
Here's something else, Don.

00:12:58.033 --> 00:13:00.266
Congenital syphilis.

00:13:00.266 --> 00:13:02.066
Look at this baby.

00:13:02.066 --> 00:13:10.099
Its mother infected it before it was born because 
she had syphilis and didn't get treated.

00:13:10.100 --> 00:13:13.966
Now, you say there is no other girl, Don.

00:13:13.966 --> 00:13:18.899
But if you're lying to protect a girl, just consider 
what it might cost her.

00:13:18.900 --> 00:13:20.466
[Don:] But she might not even have it.

00:13:20.466 --> 00:13:25.299
[Dr. Carlson:] You can't take that risk. Only a 
doctor can tell you for sure.

00:13:25.300 --> 00:13:31.700
[Don:] She's a nice girl, doctor. I don't want her to 
have to go through all this if she doesn't have to.

00:13:31.700 --> 00:13:38.433
[Dr. Carlson:] All right, Don. It's your decision.

00:13:38.433 --> 00:13:45.933
But if you're the young man I think you are, you'll 
bring that girl in to see me.

00:13:45.933 --> 00:13:48.366
[Don:] I have to think about it, doctor.

00:13:48.366 --> 00:13:51.399
I've got to have time to think about it.

00:13:51.400 --> 00:14:02.900
[Music]

00:14:02.900 --> 00:14:05.500
[Don:] She might not even have it.

00:14:05.500 --> 00:14:10.000
[Dr. Carlson:] Only a doctor can tell. You can't take 
that risk.

00:14:10.000 --> 00:14:18.800
[Music]

00:14:18.800 --> 00:14:22.400
[Don, thinking to himself:] I may have given Betty 
syphilis. Syphilis.

00:14:22.400 --> 00:14:28.200
[Music]

00:14:28.200 --> 00:14:35.800
[Dr. Carlson voiceover:] She'll never know until it's too late....she goes insane or becomes a hopeless cripple.

00:14:35.800 --> 00:14:48.100
[Music]

00:14:48.100 --> 00:14:54.533
[Don walks along, thinking.]

00:14:54.533 --> 00:15:06.666
[Music]

00:15:06.666 --> 00:15:14.260
[Betty emerges from the doctor's office.]

00:15:18.100 --> 00:15:24.200
[Dr. Carlson:] Now, there's something I want to tell 
both of you. Now, what's happened is past.

00:15:24.200 --> 00:15:28.700
You both have the disease and you will both have 
to be treated.

00:15:28.700 --> 00:15:33.133
Now, you took a risk by doing something that 
society condemns.

00:15:33.133 --> 00:15:35.699
Perhaps you didn't realize some of the penalties involved.

00:15:35.700 --> 00:15:39.033
[Don:] Betty, I didn't.

00:15:39.033 --> 00:15:42.933
[Dr. Carlson:] Betty, I know that you blame Don.

00:15:42.933 --> 00:15:45.633
But you should thank him for one thing.

00:15:45.633 --> 00:15:48.633
[Betty:] Which thing, doctor?

00:15:48.633 --> 00:15:55.966
Shall I thank him for giving this to me or for adding 
me to his list of girls.

00:15:55.966 --> 00:15:58.266
Just what do I thank him for?

00:15:58.266 --> 00:16:01.366
[Don:] For gosh sakes, Betty, I didn't mean to do 
this to you.

00:16:01.366 --> 00:16:05.999
[Betty:] What is it, doctor? What do I thank Don 
for?

00:16:06.000 --> 00:16:09.833
[Dr. Carlson:] Just be thankful he brought you in in 
the first place.

00:16:09.833 --> 00:16:13.333
And be thankful he brought you before it was too 
late.

00:16:13.333 --> 00:16:15.133
Now, we've caught this thing in time.

00:16:15.133 --> 00:16:16.833
We can take care of it.

00:16:16.833 --> 00:16:20.866
You and Don are both going to be all right.

00:16:20.866 --> 00:16:31.832
[Betty:] You may be right, doctor. But right now, I'd 
rather be dead.

00:16:31.833 --> 00:16:33.866
[Dr. Carlson:] I know.

00:16:33.866 --> 00:16:37.366
But you're thinking only of this moment.

00:16:37.366 --> 00:16:41.932
Tomorrow you'd rather be cured.

00:16:41.933 --> 00:16:53.666
[Music]

